	•	Section 2 Comments/Quotes: The study included “27,860 heart transplantations, corresponding to 27,705 patients.” Recipient mean age was “52 ± 13 years,” and 76% were male, implying 24% female. Race and numerous clinical-history variables were reported, including diabetes, infection, dialysis, previous transplant, previous cardiac surgery, ICU status, ventilation, ECMO, IABP, VAD, bilirubin, creatinine, PRA, and diagnosis.  ￼

