	•	Hyperparameter Tuning Reported: Not Reported
	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper compared the deep-learning IHTSA model with the logistic-regression-based IMPACT score. IHTSA used recipient and donor tabular registry variables, whereas IMPACT used recipient variables only. The study split cohorts into pre-2009 derivation and 2009–2011 temporal test cohorts, which is best classified as external temporal validation relative to the derivation era. The text mentions CART was used by IHTSA developers to assess relative feature importance, but not as a main explainability framework in this paper. Hyperparameter tuning was not described in the retrieved text.  ￼

Section 4: AI Quality & Reproducibility (CONVINCE Standards)
